1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,300
My dad died sixteen years ago.

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:05,280
Last night, he wrote in his logbook again.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:08,712
His old Kenworth sits in my barn.

4
00:00:08,712 --> 00:00:10,000
It never moves.

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,394
But every morning, there's a new line.

6
00:00:13,394 --> 00:00:14,570
His handwriting.

7
00:00:15,170 --> 00:00:18,410
3:10 a.m. Forty-one miles.

8
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:20,960
My wife says I write it in my sleep.

9
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:22,960
So I slept in the cab.

10
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:24,580
Nothing moved.

11
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:27,040
At sunrise, there was a new line.

12
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,550
3:10 a.m. No miles.

13
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:34,090
Just four words: "Went to meet him."

14
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:37,240
My grandson was born at 3:10 that night.

15
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:41,460
The nurse said a big man in an
old trucker cap held him first.

16
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,440
He smelled like diesel.
